MEMORANDUM OF APPEAL

The Appellant above-named most respectfully submits as follows:

1. That the Sessions Court, Udaipur vide its judgment dated ______ acquitted the respondents of the charges under Sections 302, 120B and 201 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.

2. That the Appellant is aggrieved by the said judgment and seeks leave to appeal against the acquittal.

GROUNDS OF APPEAL

A. The learned Sessions Court failed to appreciate the dying declaration in proper perspective.

B. The learned Sessions Court erred in discarding the last-seen evidence on minor contradictions.

C. The learned Sessions Court wrongly rejected the FSL report based on a minor delay in chain of custody.

D. The learned Sessions Court failed to appreciate the motive established by the land dispute.

E. The learned Sessions Court erred in giving benefit of doubt when the prosecution evidence was sufficient.

PRAYER

It is therefore prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Allow the present appeal;
(b) Set aside the judgment of acquittal;
(c) Convict the respondents for the offences charged;
(d) Pass any other order as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit.

